From aaca27fb9499e99af39d0049fc6a7b7ce6bf1b26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philipp Wagner <philipp.wagner@tum.de>
Date: Wed, 17 Oct 2018 14:33:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] DEM UART: Fix remaining Linux boot issues

1) Acknowledge all bus accesses

Flow control cannot be performed through the bus, but must be performed
using the UART LSR register. Linux, for example, clears the interrupt
lines by reading the RBR (RX) register even though no data is available.
If we do not acknowledge this write (and return bogous data) the Linux
boot hangs.

2) Do not register bus_* signals. That's unnecessary and breaks the bus
logic.
---
 modules/dem_uart/common/osd_dem_uart_16550.sv | 51 +++++--------------
 modules/dem_uart/test/test_dem_uart_wb.py     | 16 ++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

